### 1. `formula_engine/parser.py` (LaTeX AST Parser)
- Formal Lexer/Tokenizer converting LaTeX string input into structured token streams.
- AST Parser supporting node classes:
  - `NumberNode`, `SymbolNode`, `GreekNode`, `TextNode`
  - `FractionNode` ($\frac{\text{num}}{\text{den}}$)
  - `SubSupNode` ($base_{sub}^{sup}$)
  - `NaryNode` ($\sum_{sub}^{sup}, \int_{sub}^{sup}, \prod_{sub}^{sup}, \lim_{sub}$)
  - `RadicalNode` ($\sqrt[deg]{expr}$)
  - `AccentNode` ($\bar{expr}, \hat{expr}, \vec{expr}$)
  - `MatrixNode` (matrix, bmatrix, pmatrix)
  - `CasesNode` (piecewise functions)
  - `ArrowNode` ($\xrightarrow{label}, \rightarrow$)
  - `DelimitedNode` ($\left( expr \right)$)

### 2. `formula_engine/omml_compiler.py` (AST to OMML Compiler)
- Traverses AST nodes recursively to generate canonical Microsoft Office Math Markup Language (OMML) OpenXML XML nodes:
  - `<m:f>` for fractions (stacked numerators/denominators with `<m:num>` and `<m:den>`)
  - `<m:sSub>`, `<m:sSup>`, `<m:sSubSup>` for subscripts and superscripts
  - `<m:nary>` for summations, integrals, products, and limits
  - `<m:rad>` for square roots ($\sqrt{n}$) and $n$-th roots
  - `<m:acc>` for accent bars ($\bar{x}$) and hats ($\hat{x}$)
  - `<m:m>`, `<m:mr>`, `<m:e>` for matrices and cases
  - `<m:d>` with delimiter characters for cases and parenthesis groupings
  - Cambria Math typography preservation across display (`<m:oMathPara>`) and inline (`<m:oMath>`) math containers.

### 3. `formula_engine/validator.py` (Validation & Export Gatekeeper)
- `validate_docx_xml(docx_path)`: Unzips the generated `.docx`, extracts `word/document.xml`, and performs a deep regex/tree scan for forbidden raw LaTeX commands (`\frac`, `\sum`, `\lambda`, `\epsilon`, `\text{`, `\rightarrow`, `\alpha`, `\beta`, `\gamma`, `\Delta`, `\%`, `\_`, `\^`, `_{`, `^{`) and corrupted Unicode replacement characters (`U+FFFD`, `□`, `??`).
- **STRICT ENFORCEMENT**: If ANY forbidden token or corrupted character is detected in `<w:t>` elements, the validator immediately raises a `ValidationError` and halts PDF export.
- `validate_omml_structure(docx_path)`: Asserts that every math block is encapsulated inside valid `<m:oMath>` or `<m:oMathPara>` nodes and contains no empty boxes.
- `validate_pdf(pdf_path)`: Inspects exported PDF binary/text for rendering parity and complete symbol resolution.

### 4. `formula_engine/tests/test_formula_engine.py` (Automated Regression Test Suite)
- Test suite executing 100+ equations testing:
  - Simple & nested fractions
  - Summations, integrals, products, limits
  - Matrices (bmatrix, pmatrix, matrix)
  - Piecewise cases
  - Greek alphabet ($\alpha, \beta, \gamma, \delta, \epsilon, \lambda, \mu, \sigma, \Delta, \Sigma$)
  - Accents ($\bar{x}, \hat{x}, \vec{x}$)
  - Subscripts & superscripts
  - Inline math & display math
  - Equations inside table cells and figure captions
  - Equation right-aligned numbering tags `(1)`–`(5)`.

### 5. `formula_engine/publisher.py` (IEEE Document Generator)
- End-to-end publisher compiling `paper2_academic_universe_growth_intelligence.md` into `Academic_Universe_Paper2_v1.0_IEEE_Final_OMML.docx` and `.pdf`.
- Automatically executes the validation layer post-generation.

